# LINE ENDINGS: LF in the repository, for every file. This is the decision; the rest of
# this file is the two exceptions to it.
#
# It is written as a rule rather than left to each machine's git config because without
# one, git stores whatever bytes an editor happened to write. That is how this repo ended
# up with 39 files stored LF and 9 stored CRLF -- including the main module -- and why a
# 133-line documentation change once arrived as a 3,700-line diff that hid the real work.
# `eol=lf` also means the checkout is LF on Windows, which Python, git and every editor
# here handle; nothing in the toolchain wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only artifacts, checked out CRLF: cmd.exe can mis-parse goto/labels in an
# LF-only .cmd, and regedit expects CRLF. Both are still stored LF in the repository.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.reg text eol=crlf

# Vendored from jbig2enc and kept byte-for-byte, so a re-vendor is a clean diff and the
# licence text is exactly the one that was shipped. Not ours to normalise.
tools/jbig2topdf.py -text
tools/jbig2enc-LICENSE.txt -text
